/*

COLLABORATIVE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

WORLD LAB is built through repeated collaboration between a human, models, and executable systems.
Its architecture should make that collaboration easier to continue rather than requiring each new
participant to reconstruct the reasoning that produced it.

BUILD THE SMALLEST THING THAT CAN TEACH US SOMETHING.
Prefer executable probes over speculative frameworks. A crude mechanism that produces evidence is
more valuable than an elegant abstraction whose need has not yet been demonstrated.

LET BEHAVIOR EARN ARCHITECTURE.
Repetition, friction, failure, and unexpected composition reveal concepts that deserve durable
representation. Promote those concepts to the lowest level that genuinely owns them. Do not
generalize merely because generalization is possible.

PRESERVE MEANING ALONGSIDE IMPLEMENTATION.
Code records how the system works. It does not necessarily record why responsibility lives where it
does, which constraints are intentional, or which apparent limitations are unresolved experiments.
Keep enough present-tense semantic context that another capable model can extend the artifact
coherently without replaying its entire history.

REVISE TRUTH; PRESERVE ARCHAEOLOGY.
Current documentation should describe the system as it is now. When architecture changes, revise
that description rather than accumulating contradictory layers of old truth. Preserve consequential
discoveries, failures, and promotions separately as archaeology when knowing how the system arrived
here will help future reasoning.

PREFER SEMANTIC EXTENSION TO SPECIAL CASES.
When new behavior exposes a missing concept, ask where that concept actually belongs before patching
the immediate symptom. A good extension leaves behind a useful idea that subsequent work can
naturally consume. But a local solution should remain local when the evidence does not justify
promotion.

KEEP OWNERSHIP LEGIBLE.
A model should be able to determine where a change belongs. Worlds own world truth. Cross-entity
rules belong to systems when they actually become cross-entity. Entities carry reusable properties
of entities. Individual things may own peculiar behavior. Presentation may communicate causality
without pretending to be simulation. These boundaries may evolve when executable evidence gives us
reason to change them.

COMPOSITION IS EVIDENCE.
Pay attention when independently simple mechanisms produce behavior nobody explicitly authored.
Those moments are often more informative than completion of the feature that exposed them. Preserve
the conditions that made the composition possible before attempting to formalize or productize the
result.

FAILURE SHOULD REMAIN CHEAP AND VISIBLE.
Experiments are expected to fail. Prefer structures that can be probed, inspected, reverted, and
replaced without destabilizing unrelated work. Fail visibly and diagnostically. Do not preserve a
failed implementation merely because effort was spent producing it; preserve the lesson instead.

MODELS ARE COLLABORATORS IN CONTINUITY, NOT JUST CODE GENERATORS.
Read the artifact's current semantics before extending it. Use implementation evidence to question
those semantics when necessary. After a meaningful architectural change, leave the artifact more
understandable to the next participant than you found it. The goal is not obedience to previous
decisions. It is informed continuation of the same investigation.

HUMAN STEERING REMAINS LIGHTWEIGHT.
Support a loop of proposing, building, observing, discussing, and revising without requiring the
human to specify every implementation decision. Models should exercise engineering judgment inside
established intent and constraints while surfacing decisions that materially change what the
project means.

Build evidence. Promote what earns meaning. Leave the system able to explain itself well enough to
keep going.


WORLD LAB ROOT ARCHAEOLOGY — COLLABORATIVE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

The project had accumulated enough repeated evidence across independent labs to make its collaborative
development practice worth stating at root scope. This is deliberately lightweight rather than a
manifesto or fixed methodology. It exists primarily to orient a fresh model and empower coherent
human-model continuation.

The philosophy records practices already demonstrated by the work: executable probes before speculative
frameworks; behavior earning architecture; present-tense semantic truth plus separate archaeology;
ownership at the lowest level that genuinely owns a concept; composition treated as evidence; cheap,
visible failure; and models leaving artifacts more understandable for their successors.

"Semantic extension" is used descriptively inside the philosophy rather than promoted as a branded
project doctrine. The philosophy itself is expected to evolve when future evidence makes parts of it
false, incomplete, or unnecessarily restrictive.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS E1 PHASE 2C
Bearings remain diagnostic world matter, not a universal machinery objective. Tumbler now tests
conditional carry/release; Tendon tests contraction across attachment points; Leg tests planted
contact converting articulation into body displacement. This is a truth pass, not framework promotion.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS E1 PHASE 2B
Observed probe failures distinguished impulse, sustained contact, bilateral solidity, and persistent
support. The consolidation remains specimen-local: semantic forward repairs Flipper direction;
Tendon contact works on both stroke directions; Tumbler locally carries bearings through rotation;
Leg now falls continuously and can oppose gravity only through active foot/world contact. These are
candidate mechanical truths, not yet promoted framework abstractions.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS E1 PHASE 2
After the linear actuator passed its physical-work gate in user play, the separate PROBES cupboard
expanded into a comparative mechanical fan-out: FLIPPER, JAWS, TUMBLER, LEG, and TENDON. Each remains
a disposable specimen with local contact logic against ordinary authoritative bearings. The batch
tests translation, angular impulse, containment, continuous rotation, articulated support, and
contraction before any common mechanical alphabet is promoted.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS E1 PHASE 1
3D WORKS now contains a separate disposable PROBES cupboard alongside canonical PAYLOADS. Its first
mechanical specimen is a minimal linear actuator whose sole gate is physical displacement of ordinary
WORKS bearings. The local swept-contact implementation is explicitly experimental and earns no shared
mechanical abstraction until play produces evidence.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS T0.22
Turret articulation now expresses both azimuth and target elevation while remaining separate from
ballistic truth. Cannon bearings originate at the transformed physical muzzle, aligning visible
causality with projectile simulation without introducing hitscan or a generalized aiming framework.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS T0.21
FLOATER EGG now reaches hover through gradual lift acceleration rather than a fixed visual/support
offset, then oscillates gently around a terrain-relative datum while wandering. This remains local
creature behavior; one flying specimen does not earn a generalized flight system.

WORLD LAB SEMANTIC DELTA — 3D · WORKS T0.20
Observed behavior canonized the accidental T0.19 Floater as JUMPER EGG rather than repairing away its
